 History:
 --------

 version 3.0b (14.11.2026) done by Vesuri:
 - timing fix always on (CUSTOM2 no longer disables it, which ran the game
   too fast on fast machines)
 - CUSTOM2 is now "Enhanced framerate": the game, the wave select and the
   attract scenes drawn at up to 50 frames a second, interpolated, at the
   game's own speed (SPS 403; an A1200 with fast RAM or a faster CPU, a
   stock A500 or A1200 draws as before)
 - 68060: words and strokes no longer missing from the vector text
   (scoring page, wave select)
 - wave select: no black box cut into the WAVE 1 text and the Death Star,
   and it no longer runs faster on fast CPUs

 version 2.00 (10.08.2016) done by StingRay:
 - patch redone
 - supports 3 versions (SPS 403, SPS 2926 and SPS 939)
 - all X-Wing guns are now displayed (Mantis issue #3429)
 - timing fixed
 - new install script
 - source code included
 - using standard version numbering now
 

 Old versions by John Girvin:
    0601.1  06/2001
            - first release
            - removed initial flight control listing
            - fixed hiscore saving
            - added infinite shield trainer

    0801.1  08/2001
            - version checks moved from installer script into slave
            - uses OSEmu 20010818
            - miscellaneous installer script improvements

    R3      10/2001
            - after many complaints:
              - new, braindead simple release numbering system
              - standard distribution archive contents
              - standard installation script
            - supports a second version of the game
            - uses OSEmu 20010915

    R4      11/2001
            - supports four versions of the game
            - fixed access fault if "QUIT" was clicked
            - changed trainer key to F4


 Contact:
 --------
 If you have problems with this installation please try and get a newer
 version of this package from the WHDLoad WWW-Page. If that doesn't help try
 some Tooltypes like NOCACHE, NOAUTOVEC, EXPCHIP, NOMMU, PAL or NTSC. If
 that also fails, please inform the author via the Bug-Report-Form which
 can be accessed on the WHDLoad WWW-Page.

 For the full WHDLoad package, other installs and updates refer to:
	http://www.whdload.de/
 or	aminet:dev/misc/whdload#?
 and	aminet:game/patch/

